{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1096881-how-have-you-used-the-god-machine","id":1096881,"title":"How Have You Used the God-Machine?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-25T15:21:48-07:00","id":1096881,"title":"How Have You Used the God-Machine?","content":"I was writing about <b><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/notes/bound-in-dreams-fans-of-changeling-the-lost/the-god-machine-changeling/1299429153506083/\" target=\"_blank\">using the God-Machine to utterly revamp my long-established Changeling game</a></b> in various ways, and I got to wondering: For those of you who have incorporated it into your Changeling games, what have you done with it? Have you been able to add it to ongoing chronicles? Did you start new ones just to use it? How has it turned out for you? Or have you avoided incorporating it? If so, why?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T15:21:09-07:00","id":1096880,"title":"","content":"I was writing about <b><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/notes/bound-in-dreams-fans-of-changeling-the-lost/the-god-machine-changeling/1299429153506083/\" target=\"_blank\">using the God-Machine to utterly revamp my long-established Changeling game</a></b> in various ways, and I got to wondering: For those of you who have incorporated it into your games, what have you done with it? Have you been able to add it to ongoing chronicles? Did you start new ones just to use it? How has it turned out for you? Or have you avoided incorporating it? If so, why?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T17:58:06-07:00","id":1096923,"title":"","content":"Well, one of the best ways im my opinion is to drop hints that can sound like true fey activity. Like children going missing or other such cases of people vanishing and sometimes coming back different. The thing is, it only seems like true fey at first but as they look into it things just get weirder and weirder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T17:58:22-07:00","id":1096925,"title":"","content":"Interesting use for the Godmachine in a Changeling game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T18:47:47-07:00","id":1096945,"title":"","content":"If it's adding Demon/GM to Changeling as a supplement, without the two being equal, I'd have the Machine be a manifestation of Iron.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T14:49:47-07:00","id":1097307,"title":"","content":"I've only used the rules update, not the metaplot as it didn't fit the tone of my campaigns","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5435-mhicwombat","name":"MhicWombat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T20:16:33-07:00","id":1097674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MhicWombat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1096881-how-have-you-used-the-god-machine?p=1097307#post1097307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've only used the rules update, not the metaplot as it didn't fit the tone of my campaigns</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no metaplot, as has been pointed out multiple times. The God-Machine existing as a widespread set of conspiracies and occult weirdness primarily encountered in the material world does not bear any more comment for its lack of inclusion in a non-Demon game than a Werewolf group's lack of Vampire characters and concepts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T09:52:48-07:00","id":1097803,"title":"","content":"I wrote up a Court once whose members pledged their loyalty to the God-Machine out of the belief that Its rigid certainty would protect changelings against the chaotic mutability of Arcadia. I never fully fleshed them out, though. Maybe I should. . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T14:13:19-07:00","id":1098237,"title":"","content":"God Machine is an exiled True Fae who successfully made a contract with Iron. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T17:15:40-07:00","id":1098288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1096881-how-have-you-used-the-god-machine?p=1098237#post1098237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">God Machine is an exiled True Fae who successfully made a contract with Iron. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>So angels are its loyalists, and the Unchained are changelings that escaped from it!<br /> <br /> No wonder demons and fairies were equated so much in folklore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T17:58:58-07:00","id":1098298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1096881-how-have-you-used-the-god-machine?p=1098288#post1098288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So angels are its loyalists, and the Unchained are changelings that escaped from it!<br /> <br /> No wonder demons and fairies were equated so much in folklore.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And why it needs so much planning in order to carry out its will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T19:40:48-07:00","id":1098320,"title":"","content":"On another note; I remember that the True Fae for some reason had trouble interacting with high-tech stuff, like being limited in the Computer Skill. If that's not what my mind just made up, maybe the God-Machine is the reason why the Gentry can't manipulate tech so easily. It's a contract between It and Them, forbidding the Gentry from hijacking the Demiurge's most favored tool on this world. Who knows what will happen by exploiting that ancient pact, or better yet, break it?<br /> <br /> Ooh, another one. Some lore on fairies say that they're angels that didn't pick a side in the battle between Good and Evil, thus being banished from both Heaven and Hell. We have Exiles, former angels of the God-Machine that somehow got cut off from It and went somewhat insane in the process. Maybe the first True Fae were Exiles? What would happen if a Stranger were to Fall completely, or be re-assimilated into the God-Machine?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T22:27:32-07:00","id":1098354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1096881-how-have-you-used-the-god-machine?p=1098288#post1098288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So angels are its loyalists, and the Unchained are changelings that escaped from it!<br /> <br /> No wonder demons and fairies were equated so much in folklore.</div> </div> </div> </div>So would one be able to the say that unchained are changelings immune to iron? After all if you look at pledges and pacts it is interesting how similar they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T23:07:06-07:00","id":1098359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1096881-how-have-you-used-the-god-machine?p=1098354#post1098354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After all if you look at pledges and pacts it is interesting how similar they are.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/400028-gmc-pledges?p=400079#post400079\">Not really</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1096881-how-have-you-used-the-god-machine?p=1098320#post1098320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another note; I remember that the True Fae for some reason had trouble interacting with high-tech stuff, like being limited in the Computer Skill. If that's not what my mind just made up, maybe the God-Machine is the reason why the Gentry can't manipulate tech so easily. It's a contract between It and Them, forbidding the Gentry from hijacking the Demiurge's most favored tool on this world. Who knows what will happen by exploiting that ancient pact, or better yet, break it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Per the section of Autumn Nightmares where the Computer limitation (which is also the Empathy and Expression limitation), the True Fae lack the ability to comprehend or create human minds and objects and thus steal and outsource ruthlessly. This fault could be the product of a long-forgotten oath with the Machine, but it could also be an internal flaw that God \u2014 notoriously sacred-and-separate-and-apart \u2014 has taken advantage of since time immemorial.<br /> <br /> (It's also worth noting that Autumn Nightmares was the first Changeling 1e supplement and the Skill limitation is starkly contradicted by later content, especially as concerns Expression \u2014 early supplements in the pre-PoD publishing schedule have something of a track record for not catching all the shifts that make up the final core product, so it's probably unwise to lean too heavily on the technological manifestations of the Others' anachronism.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ooh, another one. Some lore on fairies say that they're angels that didn't pick a side in the battle between Good and Evil, thus being banished from both Heaven and Hell. We have Exiles, former angels of the God-Machine that somehow got cut off from It and went somewhat insane in the process. Maybe the first True Fae were Exiles? What would happen if a Stranger were to Fall completely, or be re-assimilated into the God-Machine? </div> </div> </div>Given that we have both the plethora of outcomes the Cipher offers and the parameter-oriented reintegration process presented in the Storyteller's Guide, the importance of figuring out the Wyrd can't be understated in fleshing out this theory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T12:48:56-07:00","id":1098516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1096881-how-have-you-used-the-god-machine?p=1098320#post1098320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ooh, another one. Some lore on fairies say that they're angels that didn't pick a side in the battle between Good and Evil, thus being banished from both Heaven and Hell.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, according to <b>Overly Sarcastic Productions,</b> that description is the work of Christian missionaries attempting to force their religion upon the Celts without pissing them off. They downgraded the fairies and gods of the mythology into being angels, demons, or saints with great magical power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-30-2017, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T13:42:15-07:00","id":1098542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1096881-how-have-you-used-the-god-machine?p=1098516#post1098516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, according to <b>Overly Sarcastic Productions,</b> that description is the work of Christian missionaries attempting to force their religion upon the Celts without pissing them off. They downgraded the fairies and gods of the mythology into being angels, demons, or saints with great magical power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know very much about Overly Sarcastic Productions, but this is not entirely true. There is actually exceptionally little what I would call demonizing of the local pre-Christian entities with the arrival of Christianity in Ireland according to all sources we have remaining of the period. There are even <i>incredibly heretical</i> phases where it is suggested that there are gods who are lesser divinities compared to God. The only solid instance of outright potential demonizing of local entities would be in the figure of Crom Cruach, but there is a very good argument that the entire scene is not actually discussing a pre-Christian entity, but instead just a long winded biblical reference.<br /> <br /> The belief that fairies were some sort of 'third group,' is lacking in the Medieval Period, but arrives in the Modern period. To quote from D. H. Moutrary Read in <i>Some C</i><i>haracteristics</i> <i>of Irish Folklore</i> in Folklore volume 27, who himself is quoting one Miss B. Hunt,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Devil was admiring himself in a looking-glass, and he said, &quot;I am very beautiful. I am very beautiful. I am more beautiful than God.&quot; He went on saying this till God got in a tearing rage and turned the Devil out of Heaven. A lot of the angels laughed at this, and God was so angry at their laughing that He threw them out of Heaven also, bailing them out by handfuls. So they fell down, down, down. But St. Michael interfered and begged for them to be spared. So they were allowed to stay where they were. And some were on earth, some were in the sea, and some were in the sky. So they became the Fairy Host. </div> </div> </div>While demonizing local entities is very common with the arrival of Christianity, it is <i>very strangely</i> not evident within the early literature of the period. Lugh is not treated like Ba'al or Moloch and turned into one of the demonic host, but simply fades into traditional belief. The closest we have is Brigid <i>possibly</i> becoming Saint Brigid, but that is a really contentious issue, with a lot of evidence towards it being from the works of Gerald of Wales who we know was entirely making things up to try to justify a reconquest of Ireland by labeling them pagans. The idea of Saint Brigid being a continuation of Brigid has some roots in his works, which we now know were politically motivated lies.<br /> <br /> Edit: Thinking about this a bit more. Local Deities were probably... de-deified, or 'powered down,' but we don't have record of this happening until several hundred years after conversion. It is more likely that these works were less of an intentional erasure of local beliefs, but a recording of what could be remembered by these early scholars, or simply attempts at making some nice literature drawing on the stuff grandma used to talk about. The early Irish church was not organized enough to conspire to such great heights honestly, they were a bit ramshackle and didn't like each other very much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 05-30-2017, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}